# ==== Cargo / build artifacts (both crates) ====
**/target

# ==== Frontend build output (generated inside the docker build) ====
parser-web/dist

# ==== JS deps (installed via `npm ci` inside the build) ====
**/node_modules

# ==== Local database + media cache — tens of GB, mounted at runtime by compose ====
# The directory covers database.db together with the -wal/-shm SQLite keeps
# beside it; ignoring only the .db file would ship a multi-GB -wal into the
# build context (and `COPY parser-api/ .` would carry the media cache in too).
parser-api/data/
parser-api/media/
# A database left at the repository root (the pre-`data/` layout, or a stray
# copy) is not an input to the build either: shipping 30 GB into the builder
# stage turned a 22 s context transfer into 22 GB, ~150 s, plus a 30 GB layer
# in the build cache. `**/` so it also covers a nested copy.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# ==== Editor / IDE ====
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ==== VCS ====
.git/
.gitignore

# ==== OS ====
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ==== Pi tooling / local state ====
.pi/
.pi-subagents/

